<body><h1 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 1"'>Power Monitor Technical User Guide</h1>
<h2 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 2"'>Version 1.1.1</h2>
<h2 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 2"'>Changelog</h2>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>Version 1.1.1 (April 15, 2026)</h3>
<li>**Web Chart Improvements**:</li>
<p>  - Dynamic linear Y-axis scaling for improved detail in the normal 2-4A range</p>
<p>  - Horizontal slider retained for panning older/newer data windows</p>
<li>**Feature Cleanup**:</li>
<p>  - Gas monitoring disabled in runtime logic</p>
<p>  - CSV file format preserved for backward compatibility</p>
<li>**OTA Reliability**:</li>
<p>  - Upload response completes before reboot to reduce false failure reports</p>
<p>  - Browser reconnect flow handles reboot window more reliably</p>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>Version 1.0.5 (January 5, 2026)</h3>
<li>**RS485 Communication Improvements**:</li>
<p>  - Separated DE (Driver Enable, pin 22) and RE (Receiver Enable, pin 25) control lines</p>
<p>  - Both pins configured as Active HIGH</p>
<p>  - Implemented 3-attempt retry logic with adaptive delays (75ms, 100ms, 125ms)</p>
<p>  - Added per-field error tracking and statistics reporting</p>
<p>  - Increased inter-request delay from 50ms to 75ms for improved reliability</p>
<li>**System Enhancements**:</li>
<p>  - Watchdog timer fully operational with proper refresh in all functions</p>
<p>  - Blue LED (pin 4) now flashes on SD card write operations (100ms visible pulse)</p>
<p>  - WhatsApp reboot notifications active</p>
<li>**Web Interface**:</li>
<p>  - Fixed menu wrapping issue - all items now fit on single line</p>
<p>  - Reduced menu padding from 25px to 15px</p>
<p>  - Fixed HTML typo in ZipAllFiles menu link</p>
<h2 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 2"'>1. System Overview</h2>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>1.1 Purpose</h3>
<p>The Power Monitor is a comprehensive energy monitoring system that:</p>
<li>Monitors single-phase or three-phase AC power consumption</li>
<li>Logs voltage, current, power, energy (kWh), and temperature data</li>
<li>Stores data to SD card in CSV format (daily and monthly files)</li>
<li>Provides real-time web interface for monitoring and control</li>
<li>Sends WhatsApp notifications for critical events</li>
<li>Integrates weather data for environmental correlation</li>
<li>Supports over-the-air (OTA) firmware updates</li>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>1.2 Key Features</h3>
<li>**Real-time Monitoring**: 5-second polling interval (configurable)</li>
<li>**Data Logging**: CSV files with 20 data fields per record</li>
<li>**Web Interface**: Full-featured HTTP server with multiple pages</li>
<li>**Chart Navigation**: Dynamic linear Y-axis scaling and horizontal time-window slider</li>
<li>**Remote Notifications**: WhatsApp integration via CallMeBot API</li>
<li>**Weather Correlation**: OpenWeatherMap API integration</li>
<li>**File Management**: Download, delete, and consolidate data files</li>
<li>**OTA Updates**: Wireless firmware updates via web interface</li>
<li>**Automatic Recovery**: Self-healing WiFi and SD card error handling</li>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>1.3 System Specifications</h3>
<li>**Microcontroller**: ESP32-WROOM-DA (240MHz, 320KB RAM, 4MB Flash)</li>
<li>**Power Meter**: KWS-AC301L-100A (RS485/MODBUS interface)</li>
<li>**Communication**: </li>
<p>  - RS485 at 9600 baud (to power meter)</p>
<p>  - WiFi 802.11 b/g/n (to network)</p>
<p>  - Serial console at 115200 baud (debugging)</p>
<li>**Storage**: MicroSD card (FAT32, recommended 4GB+)</li>
<li>**Power**: 5V via USB or external supply</li>
<h2 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 2"'>2. Theory of Operation</h2>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>2.1 Main Program Flow</h3>
<p><b>POWER-ON RESET â†’ setup() Function:</b></p>
<li>Initialize serial console (115200 baud)</li>
<li>Configure GPIO pins (LEDs, switches, RS485 enable)</li>
<li>Connect to WiFi (retry with automatic recovery)</li>
<li>Start web server (routes: /, /Firmware, /Display, etc.)</li>
<li>Initialize RS485 port (9600 baud)</li>
<li>Initialize SD card (retry up to 3 times)</li>
<li>Load config.json from SD card</li>
<li>Synchronize time via NTP</li>
<li>Load weather data (if enabled)</li>
<li>Open or create daily CSV data file</li>
<li>Send WhatsApp boot notification</li>
<p><b>loop() Function (continuous):</b></p>
<li>Check timing intervals (main_cycle_ms = 5000ms)</li>
<li>Call main_programme() every 5 seconds</li>
<li>Handle web server requests</li>
<li>Monitor WiFi connection status</li>
<li>Update health check timer</li>
<p><b>main_programme() Function (every 5 seconds):</b></p>
<p>1. Check for day rollover (create new CSV file)</p>
<p>2. Check for month rollover (trigger month-end process)</p>
<p>3. Send 8 RS485 requests to KWS meter:</p>
<p>   - Voltage (0x0E)</p>
<p>   - Current (0x0F)</p>
<p>   - Watts (0x11)</p>
<p>   - Uptime (0x19)</p>
<p>   - kWh (0x17)</p>
<p>   - Power Factor (0x1D)</p>
<p>   - Frequency (0x1E)</p>
<p>   - Temperature (0x1A)</p>
<p>4. Parse and store responses in Readings_Table</p>
<p>5. Update min/max values (lowest voltage, highest current)</p>
<p>6. Append data record to daily CSV file</p>
<p>7. Verify write operation</p>
<p>8. Update weather data (if interval elapsed)</p>
<p>9. Monitor SD card space (warn if <10% free)</p>
<p>10. Loop back to loop() function</p>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>2.2 Data Acquisition Cycle</h3>
<p>Every 5 seconds (configurable via <code>config.main_cycle_ms</code>):</p>
<p>1. <b>RS485 Transaction</b> (per request, with retry logic):</p>
<p>   - Enable RS485 transmitter (GPIO 22 DE=HIGH, GPIO 25 RE=HIGH)</p>
<p>   - Send 8-byte request packet (2ms delay between bytes)</p>
<p>   - Disable transmitter (GPIO 22 DE=LOW)</p>
<p>   - Enable receiver (GPIO 25 RE=HIGH for RX)</p>
<p>   - Wait for response (timeout: 500ms)</p>
<p>   - Parse response packet</p>
<p>   - Extract data value</p>
<p>   - Apply scaling factor</p>
<p>   - <b>Retry Logic</b>: Up to 3 attempts per request with adaptive delays (75-125ms)</p>
<p>   - <b>Error Tracking</b>: Per-field failure statistics reported every 10 failures</p>
<p>2. <b>Data Processing</b>:</p>
<p>   - Store in <code>Readings_Table[8]</code> structure array</p>
<p>   - Calculate derived values (averages, trends)</p>
<p>   - Update min/max tracking variables</p>
<p>   - Format values for CSV output</p>
<p>3. <b>Storage</b>:</p>
<p>   - Flash blue LED (SD activity indicator)</p>
<p>   - Open daily CSV file in append mode</p>
<p>   - Write comma-separated record (20 fields)</p>
<p>   - Verify write operation</p>
<p>   - Close file</p>
<p>   - Update file size tracking</p>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>2.3 Timing and Intervals</h3>
<table border='1' style='border-collapse:collapse'>
<tr><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>Task</th><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>Default Interval</th><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>Configurable</th><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>Main cycle</td><td style='padding:4px'>5000ms (5 sec)</td><td style='padding:4px'>Yes</td><td style='padding:4px'>Data sampling rate</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>Weather update</td><td style='padding:4px'>600000ms (10 min)</td><td style='padding:4px'>Yes</td><td style='padding:4px'>API query frequency</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>Health check</td><td style='padding:4px'>60000ms (1 min)</td><td style='padding:4px'>Yes</td><td style='padding:4px'>System diagnostics</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>WiFi retry</td><td style='padding:4px'>30000ms (30 sec)</td><td style='padding:4px'>No</td><td style='padding:4px'>Connection recovery</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>SD retry delay</td><td style='padding:4px'>1000ms (1 sec)</td><td style='padding:4px'>No</td><td style='padding:4px'>File operation retry</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>WhatsApp debounce</td><td style='padding:4px'>1000ms (1 sec)</td><td style='padding:4px'>No</td><td style='padding:4px'>Message rate limit</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>WhatsApp dup block</td><td style='padding:4px'>300000ms (5 min)</td><td style='padding:4px'>No</td><td style='padding:4px'>Prevent spam</td></tr>
</table>
<h2 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 2"'>3. Hardware Architecture</h2>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>3.1 ESP32 Pin Assignments</h3>
<table border='1' style='border-collapse:collapse'>
<tr><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>GPIO Pin</th><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>Function</th><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>Direction</th><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>2</td><td style='padding:4px'>Onboard LED</td><td style='padding:4px'>Output</td><td style='padding:4px'>ESP32 module status LED</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>4</td><td style='padding:4px'>Blue LED</td><td style='padding:4px'>Output</td><td style='padding:4px'>SD card activity indicator</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>5</td><td style='padding:4px'>SS (CS)</td><td style='padding:4px'>Output</td><td style='padding:4px'>SD card SPI chip select</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>16</td><td style='padding:4px'>RS485 RX</td><td style='padding:4px'>Input</td><td style='padding:4px'>RS485 receive from KWS meter</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>17</td><td style='padding:4px'>RS485 TX</td><td style='padding:4px'>Output</td><td style='padding:4px'>RS485 transmit to KWS meter</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>18</td><td style='padding:4px'>SCK</td><td style='padding:4px'>Output</td><td style='padding:4px'>SD card SPI clock</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>19</td><td style='padding:4px'>MISO</td><td style='padding:4px'>Input</td><td style='padding:4px'>SD card SPI data in</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>21</td><td style='padding:4px'>Reserved</td><td style='padding:4px'>Input</td><td style='padding:4px'>Reserved (gas feature disabled)</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>22</td><td style='padding:4px'>RS485 DE</td><td style='padding:4px'>Output</td><td style='padding:4px'>RS485 Driver Enable (TX ctrl)</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>23</td><td style='padding:4px'>MOSI</td><td style='padding:4px'>Output</td><td style='padding:4px'>SD card SPI data out</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>25</td><td style='padding:4px'>RS485 RE</td><td style='padding:4px'>Output</td><td style='padding:4px'>RS485 Receiver Enable (RX ctrl)</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>26</td><td style='padding:4px'>Green LED</td><td style='padding:4px'>Output</td><td style='padding:4px'>Status indicator</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>27</td><td style='padding:4px'>Yellow Switch</td><td style='padding:4px'>Input</td><td style='padding:4px'>User input button</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>32</td><td style='padding:4px'>Blue Switch</td><td style='padding:4px'>Input</td><td style='padding:4px'>User input button</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>33</td><td style='padding:4px'>Red Switch</td><td style='padding:4px'>Input</td><td style='padding:4px'>User input button</td></tr>
</table>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>3.2 Hardware Connections</h3>
<h4 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 4"'>KWS-AC301L-100A Power Meter</h4>
<li>**Interface**: RS485 (differential signaling, A/B twisted pair)</li>
<li>**Protocol**: MODBUS RTU variant</li>
<li>**Baud Rate**: 9600 bps, 8N1 (8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit)</li>
<li>**Slave Address**: 0x02</li>
<li>**Wiring**:</li>
<p>  - ESP32 GPIO 17 (TX) â†’ RS485 transceiver DI</p>
<p>  - ESP32 GPIO 16 (RX) â†’ RS485 transceiver RO</p>
<p>  - ESP32 GPIO 22 (DE) â†’ RS485 transceiver DE (Driver Enable - Active HIGH)</p>
<p>  - ESP32 GPIO 25 (RE) â†’ RS485 transceiver RE (Receiver Enable - Active HIGH)</p>
<p>  - RS485 A â†’ KWS meter A terminal</p>
<p>  - RS485 B â†’ KWS meter B terminal</p>
<li>**Note**: DE and RE are separate pins (both Active HIGH). During TX: both HIGH. During RX: DE=LOW, RE=HIGH.</li>
<h4 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 4"'>SD Card Module</h4>
<li>**Interface**: SPI (Serial Peripheral Interface)</li>
<li>**Format**: FAT32</li>
<li>**Recommended Size**: 4GB or larger</li>
<li>**Wiring**:</li>
<p>  - GPIO 5 (SS)  SD card CS</p>
<p>  - GPIO 18 (SCK)  SD card CLK  </p>
<p>  - GPIO 19 (MISO)  SD card DO</p>
<p>  - GPIO 23 (MOSI)  SD card DI</p>
<p>  - 3.3V  SD card VCC</p>
<p>  - GND  SD card GND</p>
<h2 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 2"'>4. Software Architecture</h2>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>4.1 Data Structures</h3>
<h4 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 4"'>RuntimeConfig Structure</h4>
<p>Location: Lines 329-345 in Power_Monitor.ino</p>
<p><code>`</code>cpp</p>
<p>struct RuntimeConfig {</p>
<p>    String wifi_ssid;              // WiFi network name</p>
<p>    String wifi_password;          // WiFi password</p>
<p>    String ntp_server;             // Time server (e.g., pool.ntp.org)</p>
<p>    String weather_city;           // City for weather data</p>
<p>    String weather_region;         // Region code (e.g., "uk")</p>
<p>    bool weather_enabled;          // Enable/disable weather fetching</p>
<p>    bool whatsapp_enabled;         // Enable/disable WhatsApp notifications</p>
<p>    int debug_level;               // 0=none, 1=errors, 2=info, 3=verbose</p>
<p>    unsigned long main_cycle_ms;   // Data sampling interval (default: 5000)</p>
<p>    unsigned long weather_update_ms; // Weather update interval (default: 600000)</p>
<p>    unsigned long health_check_ms; // Health check interval (default: 60000)</p>
<p>    String ota_username;           // OTA login username (default: "SteveG")</p>
<p>    String ota_password;           // OTA login password (default: "W00dle1gh")</p>
<p>};</p>
<p><code>`</code></p>
<h4 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 4"'>Readings_Table Structure</h4>
<p>Stores sensor data from KWS meter:</p>
<p><code>`</code>cpp</p>
<p>struct Readings_Table_struct {</p>
<p>    double voltage;                // Volts (V)</p>
<p>    double amperage;               // Amps (A)</p>
<p>    double wattage;                // Watts (W)</p>
<p>    double uptime;                 // Operating minutes</p>
<p>    double kilowatthour;           // Energy consumption (kWh)</p>
<p>    double power_factor;           // 0.00 - 1.00</p>
<p>    double frequency;              // Hertz (Hz)</p>
<p>    double temperature;            // Celsius (C)</p>
<p>};</p>
<p>Readings_Table_struct Readings_Table[8];  // Ring buffer for 8 samples</p>
<p><code>`</code></p>
