</table>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>7.3 Gas Meter Configuration</h3>
<p>Gas monitoring is currently disabled in runtime logic.</p>
<li>The **gas_meter_enabled** key is retained for configuration compatibility.</li>
<li>CSV structure remains unchanged for historical file compatibility.</li>
<li>Runtime gas tracking and active gas monitoring behavior are disabled.</li>
<p><b>Note:</b> You can keep this key in config.json; it is currently informational.</p>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>7.4 Modifying Configuration</h3>
<p><b>Web-Based Method (Recommended):</b></p>
<p>1. Navigate to <code>http://<ESP32_IP>/ConfigUpload</code></p>
<p>2. Click <b>"Download config.json"</b> to download current configuration to your PC</p>
<p>3. Edit the file on your PC using any text editor (Notepad, VS Code, etc.)</p>
<p>4. Maintain valid JSON format (proper quotes, commas, brackets)</p>
<p>5. Return to <code>http://<ESP32_IP>/ConfigUpload</code></p>
<p>6. Click <b>"Choose File"</b> and select your edited config.json</p>
<p>7. Click <b>"Upload and Reboot"</b></p>
<p>8. System will:</p>
<p>   - Validate the file (checks for required fields: wifi_ssid, wifi_password)</p>
<p>   - Backup old config to <code>config_backup.json</code></p>
<p>   - Install new configuration</p>
<p>   - Reboot automatically to apply changes</p>
<p><b>Manual SD Card Method (If ESP32 Not Accessible):</b></p>
<p>1. Power off ESP32</p>
<p>2. Remove SD card and insert into computer</p>
<p>3. Open <code>/config.json</code> with text editor</p>
<p>4. Edit values (maintain valid JSON format!)</p>
<p>5. Save file</p>
<p>6. Safely eject SD card</p>
<p>7. Reinsert into ESP32</p>
<p>8. Power on (new config loaded automatically)</p>
<p><b>Important Notes:</b></p>
<li>If config.json is missing or corrupted, the system creates a new default config.json automatically</li>
<li>Old configuration is backed up to `config_backup.json` when using web upload</li>
<li>Invalid configurations will be rejected with error message</li>
<li>ESP32 reboots automatically after successful upload to apply new settings</li>
<h2 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 2"'>8. KWS-AC301L Protocol</h2>
<p><b>MODBUS RTU Communication:</b></p>
<li>Baud: 9600, 8N1</li>
<li>Slave Address: 0x02</li>
<li>Function: 0x03 (Read Holding Registers)</li>
<p><b>8 Active Commands (Lines 560-569):</b></p>
<table border='1' style='border-collapse:collapse'>
<tr><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>Register</th><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>Command</th><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>Data</th><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>Units</th><th style='background:#DDD;padding:4px'>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>0x0E</td><td style='padding:4px'>Voltage</td><td style='padding:4px'>Ã·10</td><td style='padding:4px'>V</td><td style='padding:4px'>Line voltage</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>0x0F</td><td style='padding:4px'>Current</td><td style='padding:4px'>Ã·1000</td><td style='padding:4px'>A</td><td style='padding:4px'>Current draw</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>0x11</td><td style='padding:4px'>Power</td><td style='padding:4px'>Ã·10</td><td style='padding:4px'>W</td><td style='padding:4px'>Active power</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>0x19</td><td style='padding:4px'>Uptime</td><td style='padding:4px'>Ã—1</td><td style='padding:4px'>min</td><td style='padding:4px'>Operating time</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>0x17</td><td style='padding:4px'>Energy</td><td style='padding:4px'>Ã·1000</td><td style='padding:4px'>kWh</td><td style='padding:4px'>Cumulative energy</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>0x1D</td><td style='padding:4px'>PF</td><td style='padding:4px'>Ã·100</td><td style='padding:4px'>0-1</td><td style='padding:4px'>Power factor</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>0x1E</td><td style='padding:4px'>Freq</td><td style='padding:4px'>Ã·10</td><td style='padding:4px'>Hz</td><td style='padding:4px'>Line frequency</td></tr>
<tr><td style='padding:4px'>0x1A</td><td style='padding:4px'>Temp</td><td style='padding:4px'>Ã—1</td><td style='padding:4px'>Â°C</td><td style='padding:4px'>Sensor temp</td></tr>
</table>
<p><b>Reset Capability:</b> âŒ NOT IMPLEMENTED. KWS_Protocol.h shows write password (0x00) exists but no web interface for resetting energy counter. Would require password unlock + write command implementation.</p>
<h2 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 2"'>9. Data Flow and Storage</h2>
<p><b>Daily Files:</b> <code>DF_YYYYMMDD.csv</code> (created at midnight)</p>
<p><b>Monthly Files:</b> <code>MF_MM.csv</code> (auto-created 1st of month)</p>
<p><b>CSV Format (20 fields):</b></p>
<p><code>`</code></p>
<p>Date,Time,V1,V2,V3,A1,A2,A3,Eff Temp,Wattage,KWH,Hz,Pwr Factor,Time Stamp,Weather Temp,Feels Like,Max Temp,Min Temp,Pressure,Humidity,Wind Speed,Direction,Gas Volume</p>
<p><code>`</code></p>
<p><b>Sampling:</b> Every 5 seconds = ~17,280 records/day</p>
<p><b>Month-End Process:</b></p>
<p>1. Midnight on 1st triggers consolidation</p>
<p>2. All daily files merged into MF_MM.csv</p>
<p>3. Daily files auto-deleted</p>
<p>4. WhatsApp notifications sent</p>
<p>5. ~50MB space freed per month</p>
<h2 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 2"'>10. Function Reference</h2>
<p><b>Core Functions:</b></p>
<li>`setup()` - Initialize all subsystems</li>
<li>`loop()` - Event handler + timing</li>
<li>`main_programme()` - Data acquisition cycle (every 5 sec)</li>
<li>`Send_Request()` - RS485 transmit</li>
<li>`Receive()` - RS485 receive + parse</li>
<li>`Write_New_Data_Record_to_Data_Files()` - Append CSV</li>
<li>`Create_New_Data_File()` - New daily file</li>
<li>`ZipAllFilesToSD()` - Monthly consolidation</li>
<li>`Send_WhatsApp_Message()` - Notifications</li>
<li>`Get_Time()` - NTP sync</li>
<li>`Get_Weather()` - API fetch</li>
<p><b>Web Handlers:</b></p>
<li>`i_Display()` - Main dashboard</li>
<li>`i_Information()` - System info</li>
<li>`i_Download_Files()` - File list</li>
<li>`i_Delete_Files()` - File management</li>
<li>`i_Web_Reset()` - Remote reboot</li>
<li>`i_WhatsApp()` - Test message</li>
<li>`get_loginIndex()` - OTA login (dynamic)</li>
