<h2 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 2"'>13. Troubleshooting</h2>
<p><b>Won't Boot:</b> Check power supply (5V 1A), USB cable, try re-flash</p>
<p><b>No WiFi:</b> Verify SSID/password in config.json, use 2.4GHz network, check signal strength</p>
<p><b>No SD Card:</b> Format as FAT32, use 4-32GB card, check insertion, verify SPI wiring</p>
<p><b>No Data Logging:</b> Check RS485 connections (A/B), verify KWS meter powered, check baud rate</p>
<p><b>WhatsApp Fails:</b> Verify phone/API key in code (lines 1843-1845), check internet, test with /WhatsApp button</p>
<p><b>OTA Fails:</b> Verify credentials (config.json), rebuild firmware (<code>pio run</code>), check WiFi signal</p>
<p><b>Debug:</b> Set <code>debug_level: 3</code> in config.json for verbose console logging (115200 baud)</p>
<h2 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 2"'>14. Advanced Operations</h2>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>KWS Meter Reset</h3>
<p><b>Status:</b> âŒ NOT CURRENTLY AVAILABLE</p>
<p><b>Research:</b> KWS_Protocol.h shows write password register (0x00, command 0x37) exists, suggesting write capability for resetting energy counters, but:</p>
<li>No web interface implemented</li>
<li>No write functions coded</li>
<li>Requires password unlock sequence</li>
<li>Needs thorough testing</li>
<li>May violate metering regulations</li>
<p><b>To Implement:</b> Would need unlock function + MODBUS write command + web route + safety confirmations</p>
<h3 style='mso-style-name:"Heading 3"'>Remote Access</h3>
<p><b>Options:</b></p>
<p>1. Port forwarding (simple, less secure)</p>
<p>2. VPN (recommended - WireGuard/OpenVPN)</p>
<p>3. Cloud tunnel (ngrok, Cloudflare Tunnel)</p>
